  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:7d328f0cbd5b09b10c6c097eafdd49c1cfce8a9cbb16664629e3853a20e88e03",
      "text": "RTPP is not exposed for monitoring through the Atlas Administration API, although project settings can enable or disable it through that API. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/monitoring-alerts.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:05a2362777f8462b903454df93975f836cffff2fa4e989dbd43ab396c96de9f4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:ef98ae05a11854bf2c692db5dd459cd2f81af72771d462adaaaf8d9338e1acee",
      "text": "Query-targeting ratios are diagnostic clues; MongoDB Search change-stream cursors can raise these ratios and trigger alerts. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/real-time-performance-panel.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:04de84a5ace18c24f2017a490e5ae7e124c6b15bdec65fe69ab44fb352311144"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:b02d4fdd3f924a47c07fcde4d83588b0ee67dc4eb51ac34a7e7b96fe875033b4",
      "text": "Use RTPP during a reproducible slow request to locate resource spikes and active operations, then investigate query details separately. A published aggregation experiment demonstrates this workflow. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/monitoring-alerts.md",
      "also": [
        "https://nljug.org/foojay/why-mirroring-production-in-dev-helps-you-avoid-costly-mistakes/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:97038b171d6a2f6b726204fec8f175800d50b224505181787e05cb2772ca8043"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:ae459d322e469630ab4ca90feae91e992cbdf58cba783f70b5731de2988eae6c",
      "text": "RTPP may fail when db.currentOp() output exceeds its 4 MB per-sample maximum. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/real-time-performance-panel.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:6a0719982b3e3468f1a6eacbc725daef4128fd36512bfcd6542a7918999b37e8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:458a74ba42ed28c9c5b16fbfd32be824f69e27ee6a3032a8ebc6a6b7d4093d6b",
      "text": "Atlas documents one-second RTPP granularity. The Administration API can enable or disable RTPP, but cannot monitor its live panel data. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/monitoring-alerts.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:926af4c1fd3199def8753e5930f92cbb36dec8f1d599ef08e6724c8b1b02d0d0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:1eb0344a0b2c5576ba5c2fb1184b16161fcfec796885f2d3a4789237c4570eea",
      "text": "RTPP targets ongoing operations; Atlas separately describes Query Profiler as providing historical slow-operation samples for up to seven days. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/real-time-performance-panel.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/monitoring-alerts.md",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/analyze-slow-queries.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:1d75cf7586582870ce3752ca252104b432f9f1c70776d7aa67143fdbcaa5cd7c",
        "ev:e28620f311792a02c80af9b34b0a12b7f0071ae8e34bfa84f9aab169acba468e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:8171f94006bd92e843214cceed93dc0f8341c14190c6f10f1bb58811ffb2bc2d",
      "text": "COMPASS-10802 records an RTPP link returning 404 because /host/ was used instead of /metrics/. The issue was resolved with fix version 1.49.11. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-07-01)",
      "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/COMPASS-10802",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:0e40adefd5bf27dac224d5600d0062f7c558d1f99e329c0dfdcef66d6818d1cd",
        "ev:ca5618cb08b46df951d9980964052631585641cc4903d9b5ca8ee43605fd6a14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:931952cfa151cb17e1b1240e6e325862ceb40451cdcc2b73d490232cf1f9071d",
      "text": "RTPP is Atlas's live triage panel for current database operations, network traffic, and host resources; it helps correlate query latency with resource pressure. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/real-time-performance-panel.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/monitoring-alerts.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:b5880f6112f0194237c17e6e561b509dbb19dbbc8465c2a0744ab6ec9ee49a03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:e8eeb203cd16d86eab17ea62885749b34393845a2bc47890cd8361713c88832e",
      "text": "RTPP requires M10+ clusters. OneUptime and a Severalnines-authored answer independently corroborate this eligibility restriction. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/real-time-performance-panel.md",
      "also": [
        "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-use-mongodb-atlas-monitoring-for-cloud-deployments/view",
        "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/74064516/finding-mongodb-cpu-usage-disk-utilization-ram-using-query-command"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:1b2dc4a1e23562a265e185906bdda61687c348fbc0c7ea3384b8c54e813cd8e7",
        "ev:e54b2c1e42202486750c43506bca194cf3a573b253de5be58b77f4898bfb8325",
        "ev:e72ae0aea9b222ce652128009c03abb23156c5f1e42bb0fdbab9528befa56b3e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:393c15149e2414abb0ad5394d997ffc972b98a8647fe614929f923ea13ce5a0b",
      "text": "RTPP's Slowest Operations uses db.currentOp(); Hottest Collections uses mongotop, and execution-latency charts use serverStatus opLatencies. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/real-time-performance-panel.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:351098fdd87a8de8dd5008b778c30ea05fa263d2efd884bd1be9a2648fe40c98"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:31e0a752880003afdeb7b539cd30e8629ebffe1ed9370103a3755251830eb125",
      "text": "Pausing RTPP freezes its display while underlying data collection continues; resuming restarts its line graphs with an empty display. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/real-time-performance-panel.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:58484615081875af06d20b6ab3ad4add9e58d702677cb0dbe2a48e4f2eec3413",
        "ev:bf3f1afab31d0143007139e6ce8145b48f345972878959816889e5a034fe1444"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:714ef035f27fa0635ba919c0d8c563f9c5a097b3c466c987a036ae059db05031",
      "text": "The Kill Op control invokes db.killOp() on the selected running operation and requires an authorized project role. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/real-time-performance-panel.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/monitoring-alerts.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:dd41e51c8b5099e8eb7a7b66cb380204daa8d5ef041eb2e649d5dad710d368b7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:b09cb25bcda69688a2357d617348275dc2f08d073cf17e409973f695e0850a95",
      "text": "MongoDB documents one-second granularity for RTPP. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/monitoring-alerts.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:af0f9e68638c08c3494cbf60ad96b47c5b855dcdc9949b2dc23ad801deec684a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:0f38647a943b852c6a2471171028384b024661dc6cd14bab048590b136d367bb",
      "text": "RTPP uses mongostat for operation counters, mongotop for hot collections and db.currentOp() for the slowest current operations. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/real-time-performance-panel.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:1ba993c3abc030d7cdade3835bcbf752f3994cc1aba56981c5c8c291fbeca220"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:747733d6e20e7ffdc086fc2cd2985d412f607b1099e563ec6a2985a41ee53605",
      "text": "MongoDB Search change-stream cursors can inflate query-targeting ratios, so a high ratio alone does not establish an application indexing defect. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/real-time-performance-panel.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:04de84a5ace18c24f2017a490e5ae7e124c6b15bdec65fe69ab44fb352311144"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:9c15e13bb39909772509eb504b0e92d186d27e242243701900231e0514dbfdd4",
      "text": "Queryable Encryption hides affected collections from Hottest Collections and redacts query JSON involving encrypted fields. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/real-time-performance-panel.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:b2e0813aad7a0b2a31bfcfdfe28c8991c581f0926a312d88249258f5a2f0d9a9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:add174bc8c8355ae09baab2105728eac54970e7d8c0f6988200defa53cdc4ec8",
      "text": "Vokint recommends pairing Atlas live operations and cluster signals with application OpenTelemetry traces; this is an integration recommendation, not proof that RTPP provides distributed tracing. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://invokfung.github.io/blog/2025/08/19/mongo_26_opentelemetry_observability/",
      "also": [],
